From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] theme: one quiet state fill for checked controls, and ringed scale handles

Luma ADR-043. Ink is the one emphasis a view keeps (a suggested action);
every on state takes one quieter fill. Native apps (Filer, Settings, Quick
View) had three different answers for "on": a checked button was a wash of
its own ink (currentColor 30%, about 1.9:1 from the window), a toggle group's
selected segment was a raised white pill on a grey track (about 1.1:1 from
the off segments), and a scale ran its value in the accent under a white
handle on a 1px hairline. None of the three kept on and off 3:1 apart, and
the kit's own apps did something else again: a near-black block.

The state is now one set of custom properties on :root, the same values as
the app kit's luma_state tokens:

              --luma-state  --luma-state-ink  --luma-knob  --luma-knob-ring
  light       #61728a       #ffffff           #ffffff      #61728a
  dark        #8a99a8       #161a1f           #2a2e34      #8a99a8
  frost hdr   #a9b5c1       #161a1f           #1f252d      #a9b5c1
  glass hdr   #a9b5c1       #161a1f           #151a21      #a9b5c1

A checked button, raised or flat, and a toggle group's selected toggle fill
with --luma-state and write --luma-state-ink; a scale's highlight is
--luma-state and its handle is a --luma-knob disc with a 2px inset
--luma-knob-ring. Frost and glass headers are the smoked veil (0038), where
the light slate stands only about 3:1 from the veil, so they redefine the
four properties on the headerbar; window bodies keep the light values.

Measured (WCAG, composited; frost and glass over pure white and pure black),
worst case over the window, view, card, header, sidebar and popover fills and
their hover and active washes: state vs its ground 3.92:1 in light, 4.11:1 in
dark, 4.91:1 on a frost header and 4.27:1 on a glass one; glyph on state
4.90:1 light, 5.99:1 dark, 8.38:1 smoked. The ring is the state colour, so it
measures the same against the surface. Suggested,
destructive, opaque and OSD buttons keep their own fills.

Menus, in the same pass. 0024 drew a group's heading and a row's description
at 46% of the ink, a shortcut cap at 68% and a disabled row at 38%. On a
light menu the heading measured 2.59:1 and a disabled row 2.14:1. They now
take three measured colours, @luma_menu_heading, @luma_menu_shortcut and
@luma_menu_disabled:

              heading   shortcut  disabled
  light       #666c72   #666c72   #8b9094    4.95 / 4.61 / 3.01
  dark        #9ea2a6   #a7abae   #7b8084    4.75 / 4.70 / 3.06

worst case on the menu, its raised hover row and, for the shortcut, the
passive cap. The app kit redefines them for frost and glass menus (white at
60%, 68% and 40%: 5.64/5.33/3.16 frost, 5.72/5.28/3.19 glass).

Compiled with sassc against pristine libadwaita-1.9.3 plus 0001-0038.

Generated against the 0038 tree for release .48.
---
diff --git a/src/stylesheet/_colors.scss b/src/stylesheet/_colors.scss
--- a/src/stylesheet/_colors.scss
+++ b/src/stylesheet/_colors.scss
@@ -115,6 +115,11 @@
 @define-color luma_menu_border RGB(35 44 52 / 9%);
 @define-color luma_menu_shadow #0c1015;
 @define-color luma_menu_passive RGB(39 48 56 / 4%);
+// Menu section headings and descriptions, shortcut caps, disabled rows
+// (ADR-043): measured colours, not opacity of the ink.
+@define-color luma_menu_heading #666c72;
+@define-color luma_menu_shortcut #666c72;
+@define-color luma_menu_disabled #8b9094;
 @define-color luma_menu_pressed RGB(39 48 56 / 10.5%);
 @define-color luma_menu_destructive #b75048;
 
@@ -202,6 +207,9 @@
   @define-color luma_menu_border RGB(255 255 255 / 7.5%);
   @define-color luma_menu_shadow #0c1015;
   @define-color luma_menu_passive RGB(255 255 255 / 3.8%);
+  @define-color luma_menu_heading #9ea2a6;
+  @define-color luma_menu_shortcut #a7abae;
+  @define-color luma_menu_disabled #7b8084;
   @define-color luma_menu_pressed RGB(255 255 255 / 10.8%);
   @define-color luma_menu_destructive #e97870;
 }
@@ -302,6 +310,16 @@
   --active-toggle-bg-color: #ffffff;
   --active-toggle-fg-color: #1f2937;
 
+  // Filled controls (Luma ADR-043). Ink is the one emphasis a view keeps;
+  // every on state -- a checked button, a selected toggle, a view switcher,
+  // a scale's value -- takes this quieter slate, 3:1 or more from the surface
+  // and the off state, with its glyph at 4.5:1. A scale's handle is a disc of
+  // the surface ringed in it. The same values as the app kit's luma_state.
+  --luma-state: #61728a;
+  --luma-state-ink: #ffffff;
+  --luma-knob: #ffffff;
+  --luma-knob-ring: #61728a;
+
   --overview-bg-color: #f3f3f5;
   --overview-fg-color: #1f2937;
 }
@@ -311,6 +329,11 @@
     --active-toggle-bg-color: rgb(255 255 255 / 20%);
     --active-toggle-fg-color: #ffffff;
 
+    --luma-state: #8a99a8;
+    --luma-state-ink: #161a1f;
+    --luma-knob: #2a2e34;
+    --luma-knob-ring: #8a99a8;
+
     --overview-bg-color: #28282c;
     --overview-fg-color: #ffffff;
   }
